{
  "cell": "bias_core_mirror_amp",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md for",
    "the recipe this follows and layout/bias_core_mirror_amp/README.md for this",
    "cell's own floorplan/routing reasoning and results. Issue #35 (part of #34,",
    "itself a follow-on from #30/#4); the compose-cell recipe is the one",
    "layout/bias_core_pnp8_leg/ (issue #30/PR #33) established, and the",
    "multi-plane two-row CMOS shape is layout/bias_core_settle_flag/'s (#39/PR",
    "#46) and layout/bias_core_startup/'s (#38/PR #48).",
    "",
    "This is design/netlist/bias_core.spice's XMP1/XMP2/XMP3/XMPBN/XMBN/XMBN2/",
    "XMBP/XMPIB/XMPT/XMI1/XMI2/XML1/XML2/XMS2N/XMS2P device group -- the PFET",
    "current-mirror legs, the PFET/NFET bias-mirror pair, the bias-current",
    "output devices, and the PFET-input error amp with its NFET mirror load.",
    "15 devices, 10x sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 + 5x",
    "sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5, each its own single-instance `klt gen",
    "mos_array` call (rows=1 cols=1 dummy=0 gate_contact=true) -- no matched",
    "array: XMI1/XMI2 and XML1/XML2 ARE matched pairs electrically, but klt's",
    "mos_array common-centroid interdigitation draws one array as one block",
    "with shared S/D, which cannot express this group's distinct per-terminal",
    "nets (XML1 is diode-connected, XML2 is not), so each device is drawn",
    "separately and matching is left to the identical drawn geometry.",
    "",
    "None of these 15 devices is the sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40 device",
    "2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1894 blocks, so (unlike bias_core_pnp8_leg/",
    "bias_core_xq1_xqr) this group was free to reach a full klt lvs match.",
    "",
    "KNOWN GAP, disclosed here because a clean LVS match below cannot see it:",
    "`klt gen` cannot draw sky130's hvi (75/20) thick-oxide marker, so these",
    "are the 5V devices' W/L drawn in the 1.8V domain's geometry. See",
    "README.md's 'The one thing this layout does not yet say' section and",
    "2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1912.",
    "",
    "FLOORPLAN (placement.strategy 'explicit'): the two-row CMOS shape",
    "bias_core_settle_flag established. NMOS row along y=0 (orientation",
    "'none', gates facing north); PMOS row with its bottom edge at y=22.0",
    "(orientation 'mirror_y', so every PMOS gate faces south and lands on the",
    "same y=22.36 gate row -- each PMOS origin is set from its own device",
    "height, Y = 22.0 + w + 0.97); a 13um signal channel between them. PMOS",
    "column pitch is 9.0um, which leaves 1.82um between one device's own nwell",
    "island and the next one's tap -- clear of sky130's 1.27um nwell.space.1.",
    "Every PFET gets its own guard_ring nwell tap island 2.04um to its west,",
    "placed so the two nwells OVERLAP by 0.10um (one electrical node) while",
    "their li1 stays 0.20um apart, clear of the 0.17um li1 spacing floor --",
    "the same 0.10um-overlap convention bias_core_settle_flag/README.md works",
    "through. XMI1/XMI2's sources are NT, not VDD, but their BODIES are VDD,",
    "so they get tap islands too (strapped into the vdd bus like the rest).",
    "One psub tap island (add_well=false) straps the substrate to vss -- one",
    "is enough: an NMOS body is a globally synthesized net regardless of any",
    "drawn contact (see bias_core_startup/README.md's own empirical check).",
    "",
    "ROUTING (three planes, assigned per net -- and for 'n2' per LEG -- via",
    "connectivity[].layer_role / connectivity[].legs[].layer_role,",
    "klayout-tools#1655, so no two nets sharing a plane ever cross):",
    "  metal  (li1)  nbg / nt / n1 -- three local nets in disjoint x ranges;",
    "  metal2 (met1) vdd (one bus at y=65.0, ABOVE every PMOS top, with a",
    "                riser down each tap/source column), vss (one bus at",
    "                y=-6.0 below the NMOS row), pb (one channel lane at",
    "                y=18.0), and n2's ml2.D->ms2n.G leg (channel lane at",
    "                y=12.0) -- four disjoint y bands;",
    "  metal3 (met2) pg (channel lane at y=14.0), na (an 'attic' run at",
    "                y=66.0 over the whole PMOS row -- pg's own lane already",
    "                owns the channel between mp1 and mi1), and n2's",
    "                mi2.D->ml2.D leg (a column at x=88.9, east of every",
    "                block).",
    "n2's two legs live on two different planes and stitch at their shared",
    "ml2.U0_D pin through the existing via-drop: routing the whole net on one",
    "plane is not possible here (ms2n's gate sits directly under pg's own",
    "channel lane, and the mi2 end sits east of everything), which is exactly",
    "the non-planar case per-leg layer_role exists for.",
    "",
    "Every leg is steered explicitly through connectivity[].legs[]",
    "(klayout-tools#1529) rather than left to the nearest-first spanning tree;",
    "compose.response.json records routed: true for every net AND every named",
    "leg.",
    "",
    "nbtop / vref / ibias / nb touch exactly one port in this device group, so",
    "each is a pins[] declare-only top-level pin (a label on the pad's own",
    "already-drawn li1, no metal routed) rather than a connectivity[] net."
  ],
